# build artifacts relocated to D:\ArborCHI-build via junction (F: is full)
backend/.venv/

# Material bundles built from a real person's petition file.
#
# study_materials/judging_v1 is derived from a real filing under data/, which is
# itself untracked. Every exhibit in it is published material -- that is why
# exhibit group C was the one chosen -- but it is still a named individual's
# immigration case assembled in one place, and this repository is public. The
# build is reproducible from the source corpus
# (backend/scripts/build_case_bundle.py), so nothing is lost by keeping it out;
# putting it in cannot be undone. This comment does not name the petitioner, for
# the same reason.
backend/study_materials/judging_v1/

# Captured session figures. They photograph the real exhibit pages -- the same
# reason the bundle itself is not tracked. Regenerate with
# backend/scripts/capture_flow.py; the page that embeds them is built by
# backend/scripts/build_walkthrough_page.py, both of which ARE tracked.
docs/figures/flow/

# Generated exhibit material does not land in the repository on its own.
#
# It is built into TRY/ and stays there until it has been looked at and
# accepted; only then does a bundle belong here, and that is a decision to be
# made deliberately rather than by a build script choosing a path. Rendered
# pages, verification overlays and the unwarped intermediates are large and
# regenerable in any case (backend/scripts/render_exhibits.py --spec ... --out ...).
/backend/study_materials/judging_v2/
/backend/study_materials/templates/
/backend/study_materials/*/exhibits/
